{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread","id":1163716,"title":"Half-Damned errata thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-29T14:38:02-08:00","id":1163716,"title":"Half-Damned errata thread","content":"Please include your errata below. This thread is limited to reporting numerical errors, typos, visual glitches, and the like. If you have questions or would otherwise like to discuss the product, please take it to another thread.<br /> <br /> Please include a page reference for all reported issues.<br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T14:46:03-08:00","id":1163721,"title":"","content":"Using the labelled pages in book and not the pdf pages so might be off by one.<br /> <br /> P21, catss-paws should just have one s in cats<br /> P52, progrenitor should be progenitor<br /> P60, preditcable should be predictable<br /> P60, thebloody-handed needs a space between 'the' and 'bloody-'<br /> P77, insescts should be insects<br /> P93, psuedo should be pseudo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T15:12:25-08:00","id":1163732,"title":"","content":"Page 77; a dice pool refers to Deception. Should most likely be Subterfuge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T15:28:22-08:00","id":1163735,"title":"","content":"Note to self: Include brief sentence making it explicit that ghouls can learn devotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T15:51:30-08:00","id":1163739,"title":"","content":"The same picture appears on pages 97 and 120.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T16:37:38-08:00","id":1163754,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 9: </b>Vampire in Brooklyn, Blade, Angel, Let the Right One In, and Only Lovers Left Alive should be in italics instead of quotation marks (or in bold to conform with the other entries)<br /> <b>p. 12: </b>&quot;\u2014 George R. R. Martin,<b> A Game of Thrones</b>&quot;<b> -- </b><i>A Game of Thrones</i> should be in italics<br /> <b>p. 20, 32, and 107:</b> Instances of &quot;World of Darkness&quot; should be <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i><br /> <b>p. 47: </b>&quot;...<b>werewolf </b><b>Kinfolk</b>...&quot; -- should be <i>Wolf-Blooded</i><br /> <b>p. 50: </b>&quot;\u2014 Dante Alighieri, <b>\u201cInferno\u201d</b>&quot; -- <i>Inferno </i>should be in italics rather than quotation marks<br /> <b>p. 52: </b>&quot;Smile. Bow. Look pretty...&quot; -- I <i>think </i>the italicized paragraph is supposed to be in the section below (&quot;Uplifting&quot;). It awkwardly breaks up the Mikhaili backstory, and it doesn't make contextual sense for it to do so.<br /> <b>p. 53, sidebar: </b>The Mikhaili Banes don't tie to Humanity degradation (though neither do the Jiang Shi's in the core as they aren't &quot;Kindred&quot; so this might be intentional?)<br /> <b>p. 53, sidebar: &quot;</b>Favored Attributes: <b>Stamina, Manipulation</b>&quot; -- should be &quot;Manipulation or Stamina&quot;<br /> <b>p. 53, sidebar: </b>&quot;Disciplines: Animalism, <b>Fortitude</b>, Bereschligost&quot; -- Fortitude should be Resilience, the list should be alphabetical, and Bereschligost should be italicized like other unique clan disciplines: &quot;Animalism, <i>Bereschligost</i>, Resilience&quot;<br /> <b>p. 105, sidebar: </b>&quot;Drawbacks are often, but not always, <b>derangements </b>or physical flaws.&quot; -- derangements aren't a thing anymore, so it should perhaps be mental Conditions?<br /> <b>p. 116: &quot;</b>Mandragora have access to Celerity, Majesty, Resilience, and Vigor as Disciplines.&quot; -- The Large Mandrake on the next page has <i>Auspex </i>as well. The Large Mandrake also doesn't have the Skills for rolling Majesty 2 or Auspex 1 (though perhaps by design as it's just a big ole plant...)<br /> <b>p. 116-117: </b>Are the plants gaining Health/Defense boosts from Resilience/Celerity? It's not quite clear from the stat blocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-02-2017, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T16:43:39-08:00","id":1163758,"title":"","content":"pg. 47: &quot;He finds common<br /> ground with others who feel like they exist only at the behest of<br /> uncaring masters, like Proximi and werewolf Kinfolk&quot;<br /> Kinfolk aren't a thing in CofD, probably need to change that to Wolf-Blooded (likely replacing 'werewolf Kinfolk' as a whole with that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T17:08:50-08:00","id":1163764,"title":"","content":"p39, Perdition and Doom's Behest are both missing the 'header' formatting, and are instead written into the description of the preceding Twist<br /> <br /> Throughout, probably a stylistic choice and not an errata: The Ghoul &amp; Dhampir merits are all listed with headers formatted the same way as the Condition and Power ones are (similar to Numina, Dread Powers, and Conditions in ChroD core), which causes mild clarity issues - throughout the rest of Vampire (and most of 2E, I believe) merits follow a more recognizable format.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T17:12:32-08:00","id":1163768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1163735#post1163735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note to self: Include brief sentence making it explicit that ghouls can learn devotions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yes please as there was so much confusion about it from the Core Book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T18:01:42-08:00","id":1163785,"title":"","content":"<b>Pg.74</b> last paragraph: &quot;...hunting and feeding, which happens almost night.&quot; Should be &quot;nightly&quot;<br /> <b>pg.77</b> &quot; Less Damnedtonight&quot; needs a space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 12-07-2017, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T18:30:23-08:00","id":1163789,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 98: </b>&quot;Ghouls who use mortals as Touchstones...&quot; -- Ghouls don't have Touchstones; they use Integrity<br /> <b>p. 105, sidebar: </b>&quot;...every member of a ghoul family has one or two <b>Touchstones</b>...&quot; -- Related to the above: if ghoul <i>families </i>have Touchstones, it's not quite clear what the mechanics for this are (i.e., humans have bonuses for breaking points already, what level of Integrity do they attach at, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-29-2017, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T23:38:53-08:00","id":1163829,"title":"","content":"The dhampir chapter is a bit all over the place on the issue of procreation.<br /> <br /> On p13, it says the following:<br /> &quot;In the oldest and still most common way of creating a dhampir, a mortal and a vampire have sex and a child is conceived. It\u2019s rare, but it can happen, especially when the vampire approaches intercourse with the intention of having a child.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also on p13, it says this:<br /> &quot;In the mortal imagination, the mysterious hooded figure who enters a young woman\u2019s bedchamber at night is perhaps the archetypical image of a dhampir\u2019s conception. [...] This myth is misleading, as a vampire\u2019s seduction (or horrific lack thereof), no matter how erotically charged, remains impotent in regard to procreation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Later on p22, it says:<br /> &quot;No dhampir is an accident. A vampire must deliberately commit an act of monstrous occult significance to even try to conceive a human child.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, which is it? Can vampires procreate with humans or are they impotent? If they can procreate with humans, then accidents must inevitably happen (particularly if the natural expectation is that they can't get people pregnant because it's so rare), so then p22 is hyperbole at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T06:37:37-08:00","id":1163894,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6155\" data-vbnamecard=\"6155\">impernious</a>: Please also include a sentence making it explicit what order blood and Vitae are removed from a ghoul when fed on--first blood? First Vitae? Vamp chooses? <br /> <br /> Revenants' discipline give them clear flexibility but it is unhelpful to have the issue, um, obfuscated for full vamps.<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:36:59-08:00","id":1163910,"title":"","content":"The bottom edge of the cover looks as if a couple of art assets haven't been merged correctly. There's a definite line visible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T16:18:38-08:00","id":1164091,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 62: </b>&quot;...accept the <b>Blood Oath</b>...&quot; -- should be <i>blood bond</i> or <i>Vinculum</i>; Blood Oath is a <b>Masquerade </b>term.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T01:49:38-08:00","id":1164203,"title":"","content":"P.122 the insomnia merit seems Self-contradictory as it says. [The ghoul can survive with three hours of sleep, spread across as many or as few blocks as desired, within a 24-hour period.]<br /> But later say in the drawback that. [When the ghoul with this Merit sleeps, he sleeps for the full three hours unless physically shaken awake.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T05:25:44-08:00","id":1164230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1164203#post1164203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.122 the insomnia merit seems Self-contradictory as it says. [The ghoul can survive with three hours of sleep, spread across as many or as few blocks as desired, within a 24-hour period.]<br /> But later say in the drawback that. [When the ghoul with this Merit sleeps, he sleeps for the full three hours unless physically shaken awake.]</div> </div> </div> </div>The takeaway on this would just be that you can't interrupt yourself, but if someone wakes you up before those three hours are up, all you have to do is make up the difference next time you sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T06:40:49-08:00","id":1164248,"title":"","content":"Was there meant to be a Touchstone/Benefit/Drawback sidebar for the Gold family? Since the de Portocarrero are a social ghoul family I assume they get no added mechanics but the Gold family are obviously a biological ghoul family - and their resistance to Vinculum is mentioned obliquely in a sidebar but not quantified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T14:02:49-08:00","id":1164381,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 30:</b> &quot;Consider her upbringing and purpose of creation when choosing <b>Abilities </b>and Specialties...&quot; -- should be <i>Skills<