it seems to assume the nosferatu curse is the deformity one from masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T00:54:59-08:00","id":1164480,"title":"","content":"<b>p. 8:</b> &quot;Maybe he\u2019s <b>won </b>free of a regnant and on his own...&quot; \u2013 should be <i>now</i><br /> <b>p. 9:</b> &quot;<b>Salem's </b>Lot by Steven King...&quot; \u2013 should be<i> <b>'</b>Salem's</i><br /> <b>p. 13: </b>&quot;Called <b>lampijerovi[]</b>, <b>vampiri[]</b>...&quot; -- the <i>\u0107 </i>character isn't rendering<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T04:26:01-08:00","id":1164501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1164475#post1164475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P 81. The clan impostor merit seems to assume the nosferatu curse is the deformity one from masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the bane from first edition, but to be honest almost all second edition fluff completely ignores the updated bane. Just look at the art for the intro fiction to Thousand Years of Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T06:02:15-08:00","id":1164511,"title":"","content":"p21 &quot;On their part, dhampir generally find Unchained ideas of Hell and the God-Machine rather far-fetched.&quot;<br /> <br /> This makes no sense, because dhampir get every variation of the Unseen Sense merit as a built in power. Unseen Sense: God-Machine allows them to physically see Infrastructure, so dhampir should be some of the most familiar denizens of Chronicles with the God-Machine outside of Angels and Demons themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T06:56:15-08:00","id":1164517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1164511#post1164511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes no sense, because dhampir get every variation of the Unseen Sense merit as a built in power.</div> </div> </div> </div>As described in the Vampire 2e corebook, which has the same specification about supernatural concealment preventing it from tripping that allows a Mage ST to include God-Machine plots in their game without conclusively establishing the extent of that particular conspiracy's reach to a casual observer.<br /> <br /> All the usual stipulations that keep the God-Machine from being obvious despite the backdoor in Concealment Infrastructure's mystical effects apply here as in other games that aren't Demon. Dhampir generally find the notions far-fetched because generally neither demons nor the Machine are that open about their activities and the children of vampires don't have a specific inroad for the world they inhabit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T07:11:04-08:00","id":1164522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1164517#post1164517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As described in the Vampire 2e corebook, which has the same specification about supernatural concealment preventing it from tripping that allows a Mage ST to include God-Machine plots in their game without conclusively establishing the extent of that particular conspiracy's reach to a casual observer.<br /> <br /> All the usual stipulations that keep the God-Machine from being obvious despite the backdoor in Concealment Infrastructure's mystical effects apply here as in other games that aren't Demon. Dhampir generally find the notions far-fetched because generally neither demons nor the Machine are that open about their activities and the children of vampires don't have a specific inroad for the world they inhabit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your phrasing is obfuscating your point and I don't feel like arguing. <br /> <br /> To address what I <i>think</i> you're saying:<br /> <br /> Any setting where you need to care about how Dhampir interact with Unchained is a crossover setting that abides by broader rules than merely those in Vampire. One of those is that that particular variation of Unseen Sense allows the mortal to 'see the gears', is a big deal, and in every other instance where that variation of Unseen Sense comes up, such senses are life-changing and utterly un-ignorable.<br /> <br /> In such a crossover setting, it makes no sense for Dhampir to have the doubts they do.<br /> <br /> If you don't agree, that's fine, this isn't one of those places we need have shoot essays back and forth, I flagged it because I found it to be inconsistent, if the devs/writers disagree, they can just leave it as-is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T15:50:00-08:00","id":1164670,"title":"","content":"p. 81, Sire Sense should be formatted as a separate Merit, not part of Sanctioned Tracker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1164522#post1164522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your phrasing is obfuscating your point and I don't feel like arguing.<br /> <br /> To address what I <i>think</i> you're saying:<br /> <br /> Any setting where you need to care about how Dhampir interact with Unchained is a crossover setting that abides by broader rules than merely those in Vampire. One of those is that that particular variation of Unseen Sense allows the mortal to 'see the gears', is a big deal, and in every other instance where that variation of Unseen Sense comes up, such senses are life-changing and utterly un-ignorable.<br /> <br /> In such a crossover setting, it makes no sense for Dhampir to have the doubts they do.<br /> <br /> If you don't agree, that's fine, this isn't one of those places we need have shoot essays back and forth, I flagged it because I found it to be inconsistent, if the devs/writers disagree, they can just leave it as-is.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might be able to see the gears, but the higher-level concepts don't necessarily follow. &quot;Yeah, I see that pipe over there. You're saying that's part of God? Get lost.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23571-spider-queen","name":"Spider Queen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:00:31-08:00","id":1164673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1164517#post1164517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As described in the Vampire 2e corebook, which has the same specification about supernatural concealment preventing it from tripping that allows a Mage ST to include God-Machine plots in their game without conclusively establishing the extent of that particular conspiracy's reach to a casual observer.<br /> <br /> All the usual stipulations that keep the God-Machine from being obvious despite the backdoor in Concealment Infrastructure's mystical effects apply here as in other games that aren't Demon. Dhampir generally find the notions far-fetched because generally neither demons nor the Machine are that open about their activities and the children of vampires don't have a specific inroad for the world they inhabit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an errata thread, please take responses or discussions to a new thread. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:01:02-08:00","id":1164674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1164522#post1164522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your phrasing is obfuscating your point and I don't feel like arguing.<br /> <br /> To address what I <i>think</i> you're saying:<br /> <br /> Any setting where you need to care about how Dhampir interact with Unchained is a crossover setting that abides by broader rules than merely those in Vampire. One of those is that that particular variation of Unseen Sense allows the mortal to 'see the gears', is a big deal, and in every other instance where that variation of Unseen Sense comes up, such senses are life-changing and utterly un-ignorable.<br /> <br /> In such a crossover setting, it makes no sense for Dhampir to have the doubts they do.<br /> <br /> If you don't agree, that's fine, this isn't one of those places we need have shoot essays back and forth, I flagged it because I found it to be inconsistent, if the devs/writers disagree, they can just leave it as-is.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an errata thread, please take responses or discussions to a new thread. Thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:01:17-08:00","id":1164675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider Queen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1164670#post1164670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p. 81, Sire Sense should be formatted as a separate Merit, not part of Sanctioned Tracker.<br /> <br /> They might be able to see the gears, but the higher-level concepts don't necessarily follow. &quot;Yeah, I see that pipe over there. You're saying that's part of God? Get lost.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an errata thread, please take responses or discussions to a new thread. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T01:14:25-08:00","id":1165529,"title":"","content":"I suppose that &quot;Bereschligost&quot; is Russian word &quot;\u0411\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0436\u043b\u0438\u0432\u043e\u0441\u0442\u044c&quot;, which means thrift. If so, than it should be &quot;Bereschli<b>v</b>ost&quot;. Not sure about &quot;sch&quot; part either -- I'm not an expert on transliteration, but &quot;Berejlivost&quot; would probably be more pronounceable for those who don't know Russian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/120-daimon","name":"Daimon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T14:56:14-08:00","id":1165680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daimon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1165529#post1165529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that &quot;Bereschligost&quot; is Russian word &quot;\u0411\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0436\u043b\u0438\u0432\u043e\u0441\u0442\u044c&quot;, which means thrift. If so, than it should be &quot;Bereschli<b>v</b>ost&quot;. Not sure about &quot;sch&quot; part either -- I'm not an expert on transliteration, but &quot;Berejlivost&quot; would probably be more pronounceable for those who don't know Russian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say &quot;\u0411\u0435\u0440\u0435\u0436\u043b\u0438\u0432\u043e\u0441\u0442\u044c&quot; as <i>Berezhlivost</i> would be a good informal transliteration, if that's the word. That being said, <i>sch </i>is how<i> \u0436</i> would be transliterated in German, since it doesn't really contain the sound <i>\u0436</i> represents, and that would fit with the idea that the name didn't come directly from Russian to English. So <b>Berezhlivost </b>would be more accurate in English, but <b>Bereschlivost </b>would suggest it has more history.<br /> <br /> As for the g/v thing, it might be an archaism (there are cases where the \u0433-character came to represent /v/; I don't know what the circumstances/rules are), but I couldn't find any examples spelt with a Cyrillic &quot;ge&quot;, at least on Google. Or it's meant to represent a different word, but &quot;thrift&quot; fits the theme pretty well.<br /> <br /> If it's a proper errata, <b>Bereschligost </b>appears in the sidebars on pages 53 and 78.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I neither speak Russian nor am an actual linguist, I just know random crap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dar